IMPORT prelude

-- Commonwealth Entities (Payment Surcharges) Act 2024 (Cth). Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2024A00101.txt. Seat: the payer.

§ `Nouns`

-- s 4: "payment surcharge"
DECLARE `Kind of amount` IS ONE OF
    `a charge for processing the payment, on top of it`
    `a charge for one payment method rather than another`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Surcharge case` HAS
    -- s 5(1)(a)
    `the entity collects the base payment under a law`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(1)(b), s 4 "surchargeable payment"
    `another law already lets it surcharge the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount`                                        IS A `Kind of amount`
    -- s 5(2): a finding
    `the surcharge amounts to taxation`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(1)
    `the entity followed the surcharging policies`      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Surcharge position` HAS
    `this Act authorises the surcharge`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `a refund is in the entity's discretion`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `non-compliance with policy invalidates it`         IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 5(1): an entity "may charge and collect a payment surcharge in relation
-- to a payment (the base payment) if: (a) ... the Commonwealth entity has the
-- power, function or duty of collecting the base payment; and (b) apart from
-- this section, the base payment is not a surchargeable payment." (2): it
-- "must not be such as to amount to taxation". Where another law already
-- governs the surcharge, this Act does not authorise it (F1, changed after the
-- independent pass).
@ref ss 4, 5
@export May the Commonwealth entity charge me this surcharge under s 5 of the Commonwealth Entities (Payment Surcharges) Act 2024 (Cth)? Yes if it is a charge for processing my payment or for my choice of payment method, the entity has the power or duty to collect the payment under a law, and the surcharge does not amount to taxation. No where another law already lets the entity surcharge the payment (that law governs it) or the amount is not a payment surcharge. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Surcharge case`  @desc The entity's power to collect, any other surcharging law, what the amount is, and whether it amounts to taxation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this Act authorises the surcharge for` c MEANS
    JUST (    NOT (c's `the amount` EQUALS `something else`)
          AND NOT (c's `another law already lets it surcharge the payment`)
          AND c's `the entity collects the base payment under a law`
          AND NOT (c's `the surcharge amounts to taxation`))

§ `The top-level goal`

-- s 6: "may refund the whole or a part ... if the Commonwealth entity
-- believes that the refund would be appropriate". s 7(2): "A failure to
-- comply with subsection (1) does not affect the validity of a decision to
-- charge, collect or refund".
@ref ss 5-7
@export default The payer's position under the Commonwealth Entities (Payment Surcharges) Act 2024 (Cth): whether this Act authorises the surcharge (s 5); that a refund of all or part of a surcharge charged under s 5 is in the entity's discretion (s 6); and that the entity's failure to follow the Commonwealth payment surcharging policies does not invalidate its decision (s 7(2)). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Surcharge case`  @desc The surcharge facts
GIVETH A `Surcharge position`
`the surcharge position for` c MEANS
    `Surcharge position` WITH
        `this Act authorises the surcharge`             IS `this Act authorises the surcharge for` c
        `a refund is in the entity's discretion`        IS `this Act authorises the surcharge for` c EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `non-compliance with policy invalidates it`     IS FALSE
